{"strongs": "H2351", "word": "חוּץ", "translit": "chuts", "root": "חוץ", "morph": "H:N-M", "pos": "noun [masculine]", "gloss": "the outside", "definition": "חוּץ noun [masculine] the outside , sometimes, especially in plural, specifically a street, never with suffix in singular, with ָ ה locative ח֫וּצָה , חֻ֫צָה , plural חוּצוֺת , חֻצוֺת , with suffix חוּצֹתָיו etc., Isa 15:3 etc.; — 1. the outside , of a house, tent, city, camp, etc., often used, especially with prepositions, to express the adverb idea of outside, abroad (Aramaic synonym, except in sense 2 a , is בַּר , ): \\ \\ a. as accusative after verb of motion Deut 23:13 יָצָא חוּץ to go forth outside (that is, a camp), v. Deut 23:14 (as adverb accusative) בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ חוּץ outside , הוֺצִיא הַחוּץ to bring forth outside (a house or chamber) Judg 19:25 ; 2Sam 13:18 compare Neh 13:8 ; Judg 12:9 b בָּנוֺת הֵבִיא לְבָנָיו מִןהַֿחוּץ from outside , from abroad , 2Kgs 4:3 שַׁאֲלִילָֿךְ כֵּלִים מִןהַֿחוּץ from outside (opposed to בַּבַּיִת v 2Kgs 4:2 ); as genitive Lev 18:9 מוֺלֶדֶת חוּץ one born abroad (i.e. by another father or mother, of a half-sister: opposed to מוֺלֶדֶת בַּיִת ) Ezek 47:2 (twice in verse). With ָ ה locative חוּצָה , after a verb of motion Exod 12:46 מִןהַֿבַּיִת ֗֗֗ חוּצָה , Prov 5:16 חוּצָה לָעִיר outside of the city, Num 35:4 מִקִּיר הָעִיר וָחוּצָה from the wall of the city and outwards ; = on the outside, without 1Kgs 6:6 ; Isa 33:7 צָֽעֲקוּ חוּצָה cry without , 2Chr 24:8 : so הַחוּצָה Gen 15:5 ׳ וַיּוֺצֵא אֹתוֺ הח and brought him outside , Gen 19:17 ; Gen 24:29 ; Josh 2:19 +, 1Kgs 8:8 לֹא יֵרָאוּ הַחוּצָה were not seen towards the outside , Deut 25:5 לֹא תִהְיֶה אֵשֶׁת הַמֵּת הַחוּצָה לְאִישׁ זָר i.e. shall not be married into another family, compare Judg 12:9 a. \\ \\ b. with preps.: a. אלהֿחוץ towards the outside Ezek 41:9 , Ezek 34:21 pleonastic אלהֿחוצה . b. בחוץ Gen 9:22 outside (opposed to בְּתוֺךְ אָהֳלֹה v Gen 9:21 ), Gen 24:31 לָמָּה תַעֲמֹד בַּחוץ , Deut 24:11 ; Exod 21:19 אם יקום והתהלך בחוץ (after leaving a sick couch), 2Kgs 10:24 ; Ps 31:12 ; Ezek 7:15 (opposed to מִבַּיִת ), Hos 7:1 +. c. לחוץ Ps 41:7 יצא לחוץ ; = on the outside Ezek 41:17 ; Ezek 42:7 , לַחוּצָה 2Chr 32:5 towards the outside . d. מִחוּץ on ( מִן 3 c ) the outside Ezek 40:19 ; Ezek 46:2 , מִבַיִת וּמִחוּץ within and without (of an ark, building, etc.) Gen 6:14 ; Exod 25:11 = Exod 37:2 ; 1Kgs 7:9 ; Deut 32:25 מחוץ תְּשַׁכֶּלחֶֿרֶב (opposed to יּמֵחֲדָרִים אֵימָה ), Lam 1:20 (compare Ezek 7:15 above b ); so מֵהַחוּץ Ezek 41:25 . מִחוּץ לְ on the outside of , Gen 19:16 וַיַּנִּיחֵהוּ מִחוּץ לָעִיר , Gen 24:11 ; Exod 26:35 ; Exod 37:7 (twice in verse); Lev 8:17 ; Lev 14:8 ; Num 35:5 ; Josh 6:23 ; Jer 21:4 +, even after a verb of motion 1Kgs 21:13 וַיּוֺצִיאוּהוּ מִחוּץ לְעִיר , 2Kgs 23:6 , though in this case אל מחוץל is more common, Lev 4:12 ; Lev 4:21 אל מחוץ למחנה , Lev 6:4 ; Lev 10:4 ; Lev 14:40 ; Lev 14:41 + often P , Deut 23:11 . e. מִחוּצָה Ezek 40:40 on the outside , מִחוּצָה לְ v Ezek 40:44 . f. (late) חוּץ מִן outside of , Eccl 2:25 who can eat, and who enjoy, חוּץ מִמֶּנִּיִ outside of me, i.e. except me? (but read rather, with ᵐ5 ᵑ6 De Now and others, חוּץ מִמֶּנּוּ apart from, without him, i.e. God). (So Late Hebrew חוּץ מִן except, without , see De Eccl 2:25 . compare The Aramaic synonym בַּר מִן except Exod 20:3 ᵑ7 ; apart from, without Isa 36:10 ᵑ7 ; Syriac id .) 2. Of a definite locality, namely \\ \\ a. that which is outside the houses of a town, i.e. a street Isa 51:23 כַּחוּץ לַעֹבְרִים , Jer 37:21 חוּץ הָאֹפִים the Bakers' street , Prov 1:20 כַּחוּץ , (|| כָּֽרְחֹבוֺת : so Prov 7:12 ; Prov 22:13 ; Jer 9:20 ); often in plural, as חוּצֹת אַשְׁקְלוֹן the streets of Ashkelon 2Sam 1:20 , ירושׁלם ׳ ח Jer 5:1 ; Jer 7:17 ; Jer 7:34 + often Jeremiah; 1Kgs 20:34 וְחֻצוֺת תָּשִׂיםלְֿךָ בְּדַמֶּשֶׂק and streets (i.e. bazaars) shalt thou make thee in D., as my father made in Samaria (a concession involving the right of trading), Amos 5:16 ; Isa 15:3 ; Isa 24:11 (as scene of mourning), Isa 5:25 ; Jer 51:4 ; Ezek 11:6 ; Ezek 28:23 ( as filled with corpses of slain), בְּראֹשׁ כָּלחֿוּצוֺת i.e. in conspicuous places, Nah 3:10 ; Lam 2:19 ; Lam 4:1 ; Isa 51:20 , טִיט חוּצוֺת mire of streets Zech 10:5 (trampled on by warriors), in simile, of foes trodden under foot, Ps 18:43 ; Mic 7:10 ( so ׳ כְּחֹמֶר ח Isa 10:6 ), metaphor of cheapness and abundance Zech 9:3 . \\ \\ b. more generally, that which is outside enclosed cities, the open country , Job 18:17 וְלאֹ שֵׁם לוֺ עַלפְּֿנֵיחֿוּץ (see De ), compare Prov 24:27 in the plural Job 5:10 וְשֹׁלֵחַ מַיִם עַל פְנֵי חוּצוֺת , Prov 8:26 ; Ps 144:13 (as place where flocks abound).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2630')\">BDB2630</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H2351')\">H2351</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2629')\">BDB2629</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB2631')\">BDB2631</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>חוּץ</bdbheb> <b>noun [masculine]</b> <highlightword>the outside</highlightword>, sometimes, especially in plural, specifically a street, never with suffix in singular, with <bdbheb>ָ  ה</bdbheb> locative <bdbheb>ח֫וּצָה</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>חֻ֫צָה</bdbheb>, plural <bdbheb>חוּצוֺת</bdbheb>, <bdbheb>חֻצוֺת</bdbheb>, with suffix <bdbheb>חוּצֹתָיו</bdbheb> etc., <ref ref=\"Isa 15:3\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(23,15,3)\">Isa 15:3</ref> etc.; — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> <highlight>the outside</highlight>, of a house, tent, city, camp, etc., often used, especially with prepositions, to express the adverb idea of <highlight>outside, abroad</highlight> (Aramaic synonym, except in sense <b>2 a</b>, is <bdbheb>בַּר</bdbheb>, <placeholder1674/>): <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> as accusative after verb of motion <ref ref=\"Deut 23:13\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(5,23,13)\">Deut 23:13</ref> <bdbheb>יָצָא חוּץ</bdbheb> to go forth outside (that is, a camp), v.<ref ref=\"Deut 23:14\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(5,23,14)\">Deut 23:14</ref> (as adverb accusative) <bdbheb>בְּשִׁבְתְּךָ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>חוּץ</bdbheb> <highlight>outside</highlight>, <bdbheb>הוֺצִיא הַחוּץ</bdbheb> to bring forth <highlight>outside</highlight> (a house or chamber) <ref ref=\"Judg 19:25\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(7,19,25)\">Judg 19:25</ref>; <ref ref=\"2Sam 13:18\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"18\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"18\" onclick=\"bcv(10,13,18)\">2Sam 13:18</ref> compare <ref ref=\"Neh 13:8\" b=\"16\" cBegin=\"13\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"13\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(16,13,8)\">Neh 13:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Judg 12:9\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(7,12,9)\">Judg 12:9</ref>b <bdbheb>בָּנוֺת הֵבִיא לְבָנָיו מִןהַֿחוּץ</bdbheb> from <highlight>outside</highlight>, from <highlight>abroad</highlight>, <ref ref=\"2Kgs 4:3\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(12,4,3)\">2Kgs 4:3</ref> <bdbheb>שַׁאֲלִילָֿךְ כֵּלִים מִןהַֿחוּץ</bdbheb> from <highlight>outside</highlight> (opposed to <bdbheb>בַּבַּיִת</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"2Kgs 4:2\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(12,4,2)\">2Kgs 4:2</ref>); as genitive <ref ref=\"Lev 18:9\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(3,18,9)\">Lev 18:9</ref> <bdbheb>מוֺלֶדֶת</bdbheb> <bdbheb>חוּץ</bdbheb> one born <highlight>abroad</highlight> (i.e. by another father or mother, of a half-sister: opposed to <bdbheb>מוֺלֶדֶת בַּיִת</bdbheb>) <ref ref=\"Ezek 47:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"47\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"47\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,47,2)\">Ezek 47:2</ref> (twice in verse). With <bdbheb>ָ  ה</bdbheb> locative <bdbheb>חוּצָה</bdbheb>, after a verb of motion <ref ref=\"Exod 12:46\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"46\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"46\" onclick=\"bcv(2,12,46)\">Exod 12:46</ref> <bdbheb>מִןהַֿבַּיִת ֗֗֗ חוּצָה</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Prov 5:16\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(20,5,16)\">Prov 5:16</ref> <bdbheb>חוּצָה לָעִיר</bdbheb> <highlight>outside of</highlight> the city, <ref ref=\"Num 35:4\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"35\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"35\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(4,35,4)\">Num 35:4</ref> <bdbheb>מִקִּיר הָעִיר</bdbheb> <bdbheb>וָחוּצָה</bdbheb> from the wall of the city <highlight>and outwards</highlight>; = <highlight>on the outside, without</highlight> <ref ref=\"1Kgs 6:6\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(11,6,6)\">1Kgs 6:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 33:7\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"33\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"33\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(23,33,7)\">Isa 33:7</ref> <bdbheb>צָֽעֲקוּ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>חוּצָה</bdbheb> cry <highlight>without</highlight>, <ref ref=\"2Chr 24:8\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(14,24,8)\">2Chr 24:8</ref>: so <bdbheb>הַחוּצָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 15:5\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(1,15,5)\">Gen 15:5</ref> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>וַיּוֺצֵא אֹתוֺ הח</bdbheb> and brought him <highlight>outside</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Gen 19:17\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(1,19,17)\">Gen 19:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 24:29\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(1,24,29)\">Gen 24:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 2:19\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(6,2,19)\">Josh 2:19</ref> +, <ref ref=\"1Kgs 8:8\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(11,8,8)\">1Kgs 8:8</ref> <bdbheb>לֹא יֵרָאוּ הַחוּצָה</bdbheb> were not seen <highlight>towards the outside</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Deut 25:5\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(5,25,5)\">Deut 25:5</ref> <bdbheb>לֹא תִהְיֶה אֵשֶׁת</bdbheb> <bdbheb>הַמֵּת הַחוּצָה לְאִישׁ זָר</bdbheb>i.e. shall not be married into another family, compare <ref ref=\"Judg 12:9\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"12\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"12\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(7,12,9)\">Judg 12:9</ref> a. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> with preps.: <highlight>a.</highlight> <bdbheb>אלהֿחוץ</bdbheb> <highlight>towards the outside</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ezek 41:9\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(26,41,9)\">Ezek 41:9</ref>, <ref ref=\"Ezek 34:21\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"34\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"34\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(26,34,21)\">Ezek 34:21</ref> pleonastic <bdbheb>אלהֿחוצה</bdbheb>. <highlight>b.</highlight> <bdbheb>בחוץ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Gen 9:22\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"22\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"22\" onclick=\"bcv(1,9,22)\">Gen 9:22</ref> <highlight>outside</highlight> (opposed to <bdbheb>בְּתוֺךְ אָהֳלֹה</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Gen 9:21\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(1,9,21)\">Gen 9:21</ref>), <ref ref=\"Gen 24:31\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"31\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"31\" onclick=\"bcv(1,24,31)\">Gen 24:31</ref> <bdbheb>לָמָּה תַעֲמֹד בַּחוץ</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Deut 24:11\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(5,24,11)\">Deut 24:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 21:19\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(2,21,19)\">Exod 21:19</ref> <bdbheb>אם יקום והתהלך בחוץ</bdbheb> (after leaving a sick couch), <ref ref=\"2Kgs 10:24\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"24\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"24\" onclick=\"bcv(12,10,24)\">2Kgs 10:24</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 31:12\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(19,31,12)\">Ps 31:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 7:15\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(26,7,15)\">Ezek 7:15</ref> (opposed to <bdbheb>מִבַּיִת</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Hos 7:1\" b=\"28\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(28,7,1)\">Hos 7:1</ref> +. <highlight>c.</highlight> <bdbheb>לחוץ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ps 41:7\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(19,41,7)\">Ps 41:7</ref> <bdbheb>יצא לחוץ</bdbheb>; = <highlight>on the outside</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ezek 41:17\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(26,41,17)\">Ezek 41:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 42:7\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"42\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"42\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(26,42,7)\">Ezek 42:7</ref>, <bdbheb>לַחוּצָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"2Chr 32:5\" b=\"14\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(14,32,5)\">2Chr 32:5</ref> <highlight>towards the outside</highlight>. <highlight>d.</highlight> <bdbheb>מִחוּץ</bdbheb> <highlight>on</highlight> (<bdbheb>מִן</bdbheb> <b>3 c</b>) <highlight>the outside</highlight> <ref ref=\"Ezek 40:19\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(26,40,19)\">Ezek 40:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 46:2\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"46\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"46\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(26,46,2)\">Ezek 46:2</ref>, <bdbheb>מִבַיִת וּמִחוּץ</bdbheb> within and <highlight>without</highlight> (of an ark, building, etc.) <ref ref=\"Gen 6:14\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"14\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"14\" onclick=\"bcv(1,6,14)\">Gen 6:14</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 25:11\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"25\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"25\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(2,25,11)\">Exod 25:11</ref> = <ref ref=\"Exod 37:2\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(2,37,2)\">Exod 37:2</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 7:9\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"9\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"9\" onclick=\"bcv(11,7,9)\">1Kgs 7:9</ref>; <ref ref=\"Deut 32:25\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"32\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"32\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(5,32,25)\">Deut 32:25</ref> <bdbheb>מחוץ תְּשַׁכֶּלחֶֿרֶב</bdbheb> (opposed to <bdbheb>יּמֵחֲדָרִים</bdbheb> <bdbheb>אֵימָה</bdbheb>), <ref ref=\"Lam 1:20\" b=\"25\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(25,1,20)\">Lam 1:20</ref> (compare <ref ref=\"Ezek 7:15\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"15\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"15\" onclick=\"bcv(26,7,15)\">Ezek 7:15</ref> above <highlight>b</highlight>); so <bdbheb>מֵהַחוּץ</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 41:25\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"41\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"41\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(26,41,25)\">Ezek 41:25</ref>. <bdbheb>מִחוּץ לְ</bdbheb> <highlight>on the outside of</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Gen 19:16\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(1,19,16)\">Gen 19:16</ref> <bdbheb>וַיַּנִּיחֵהוּ מִחוּץ לָעִיר</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Gen 24:11\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(1,24,11)\">Gen 24:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 26:35\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"26\" vBegin=\"35\" cEnd=\"26\" vEnd=\"35\" onclick=\"bcv(2,26,35)\">Exod 26:35</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 37:7\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"7\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"7\" onclick=\"bcv(2,37,7)\">Exod 37:7</ref> (twice in verse); <ref ref=\"Lev 8:17\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(3,8,17)\">Lev 8:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 14:8\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"8\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"8\" onclick=\"bcv(3,14,8)\">Lev 14:8</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 35:5\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"35\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"35\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(4,35,5)\">Num 35:5</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 6:23\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(6,6,23)\">Josh 6:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 21:4\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(24,21,4)\">Jer 21:4</ref> +, even after a verb of motion <ref ref=\"1Kgs 21:13\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"21\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"21\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(11,21,13)\">1Kgs 21:13</ref> <bdbheb>וַיּוֺצִיאוּהוּ מִחוּץ לְעִיר</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"2Kgs 23:6\" b=\"12\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(12,23,6)\">2Kgs 23:6</ref>, though in this case <bdbheb>אל מחוץל</bdbheb> is more common, <ref ref=\"Lev 4:12\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(3,4,12)\">Lev 4:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 4:21\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(3,4,21)\">Lev 4:21</ref> <bdbheb>אל מחוץ למחנה</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Lev 6:4\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"6\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"6\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(3,6,4)\">Lev 6:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 10:4\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(3,10,4)\">Lev 10:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 14:40\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"40\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"40\" onclick=\"bcv(3,14,40)\">Lev 14:40</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 14:41\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"14\" vBegin=\"41\" cEnd=\"14\" vEnd=\"41\" onclick=\"bcv(3,14,41)\">Lev 14:41</ref> + often <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('P')\"><reflink>P</reflink></lookup>, <ref ref=\"Deut 23:11\" b=\"5\" cBegin=\"23\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"23\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(5,23,11)\">Deut 23:11</ref>. <highlight>e.</highlight> <bdbheb>מִחוּצָה</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Ezek 40:40\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"40\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"40\" onclick=\"bcv(26,40,40)\">Ezek 40:40</ref> <highlight>on the outside</highlight>, <bdbheb>מִחוּצָה לְ</bdbheb> v<ref ref=\"Ezek 40:44\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"40\" vBegin=\"44\" cEnd=\"40\" vEnd=\"44\" onclick=\"bcv(26,40,44)\">Ezek 40:44</ref>. <highlight>f.</highlight> (late) <bdbheb>חוּץ מִן</bdbheb> <highlight>outside of</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Eccl 2:25\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(21,2,25)\">Eccl 2:25</ref> who can eat, and who enjoy, <bdbheb>חוּץ מִמֶּנִּיִ</bdbheb> <highlight>outside of</highlight> me, i.e. <highlight>except</highlight> me? (but read rather, with <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Sept')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵐ5</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Syr')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ6</reflink></bdbheb></lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De</lookup> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Now')\">Now</lookup> and others, <bdbheb>חוּץ מִמֶּנּוּ</bdbheb> <highlight>apart from, without</highlight> him, i.e. God). (So Late Hebrew <bdbheb>חוּץ מִן</bdbheb> <highlight>except, without</highlight>, see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De<sup><ref ref=\"Eccl 2:25\" b=\"21\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(21,2,25)\">Eccl 2:25</ref>.</sup></lookup> compare The Aramaic synonym <bdbarc>בַּר מִן</bdbarc> <highlight>except</highlight> <ref ref=\"Exod 20:3\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(2,20,3)\">Exod 20:3</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>; <highlight>apart from, without</highlight> <ref ref=\"Isa 36:10\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"36\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"36\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(23,36,10)\">Isa 36:10</ref> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('Tg')\"><bdbheb><reflink>ᵑ7</reflink></bdbheb></lookup>; Syriac <placeholder1675/> <highlight>id</highlight>.)</div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> Of a definite locality, namely <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>a.</b> that which is outside the houses of a town, i.e. <highlight>a street</highlight> <ref ref=\"Isa 51:23\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"51\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"51\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(23,51,23)\">Isa 51:23</ref> <bdbheb>כַּחוּץ לַעֹבְרִים</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Jer 37:21\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"37\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"37\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(24,37,21)\">Jer 37:21</ref> <bdbheb>חוּץ הָאֹפִים</bdbheb> the Bakers' <highlight>street</highlight>, <ref ref=\"Prov 1:20\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(20,1,20)\">Prov 1:20</ref> <bdbheb>כַּחוּץ</bdbheb>, (|| <bdbheb>כָּֽרְחֹבוֺת</bdbheb>: so <ref ref=\"Prov 7:12\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"12\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"12\" onclick=\"bcv(20,7,12)\">Prov 7:12</ref>; <ref ref=\"Prov 22:13\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"22\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"22\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(20,22,13)\">Prov 22:13</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 9:20\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(24,9,20)\">Jer 9:20</ref>); often in plural, as <bdbheb>חוּצֹת אַשְׁקְלוֹן</bdbheb> the <highlight>streets</highlight> of Ashkelon <ref ref=\"2Sam 1:20\" b=\"10\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(10,1,20)\">2Sam 1:20</ref>, <bdbheb>ירושׁלם</bdbheb> <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Jer 5:1\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(24,5,1)\">Jer 5:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 7:17\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(24,7,17)\">Jer 7:17</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 7:34\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(24,7,34)\">Jer 7:34</ref> + often Jeremiah; <ref ref=\"1Kgs 20:34\" b=\"11\" cBegin=\"20\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"20\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(11,20,34)\">1Kgs 20:34</ref> <bdbheb>וְחֻצוֺת תָּשִׂיםלְֿךָ בְּדַמֶּשֶׂק</bdbheb> and <highlight>streets</highlight> (i.e. bazaars) shalt thou make thee in D., as my father made in Samaria (a concession involving the right of trading), <ref ref=\"Amos 5:16\" b=\"30\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"16\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"16\" onclick=\"bcv(30,5,16)\">Amos 5:16</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 15:3\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"15\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"15\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(23,15,3)\">Isa 15:3</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 24:11\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(23,24,11)\">Isa 24:11</ref> (as scene of mourning), <ref ref=\"Isa 5:25\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(23,5,25)\">Isa 5:25</ref>; <ref ref=\"Jer 51:4\" b=\"24\" cBegin=\"51\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"51\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(24,51,4)\">Jer 51:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 11:6\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"11\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"11\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(26,11,6)\">Ezek 11:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ezek 28:23\" b=\"26\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(26,28,23)\">Ezek 28:23</ref> ( as filled with corpses of slain), <bdbheb>בְּראֹשׁ כָּלחֿוּצוֺת</bdbheb> i.e. in conspicuous places, <ref ref=\"Nah 3:10\" b=\"34\" cBegin=\"3\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"3\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(34,3,10)\">Nah 3:10</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lam 2:19\" b=\"25\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"19\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"19\" onclick=\"bcv(25,2,19)\">Lam 2:19</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lam 4:1\" b=\"25\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"1\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"1\" onclick=\"bcv(25,4,1)\">Lam 4:1</ref>; <ref ref=\"Isa 51:20\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"51\" vBegin=\"20\" cEnd=\"51\" vEnd=\"20\" onclick=\"bcv(23,51,20)\">Isa 51:20</ref>, <bdbheb>טִיט חוּצוֺת</bdbheb> mire of <highlight>streets</highlight> <ref ref=\"Zech 10:5\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"5\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"5\" onclick=\"bcv(38,10,5)\">Zech 10:5</ref> (trampled on by warriors), in simile, of foes trodden under foot, <ref ref=\"Ps 18:43\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"43\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"43\" onclick=\"bcv(19,18,43)\">Ps 18:43</ref>; <ref ref=\"Mic 7:10\" b=\"33\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(33,7,10)\">Mic 7:10</ref> ( so <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>כְּחֹמֶר ח</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Isa 10:6\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"10\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"10\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(23,10,6)\">Isa 10:6</ref>), metaphor of cheapness and abundance <ref ref=\"Zech 9:3\" b=\"38\" cBegin=\"9\" vBegin=\"3\" cEnd=\"9\" vEnd=\"3\" onclick=\"bcv(38,9,3)\">Zech 9:3</ref>. <br>\\&emsp;\\&emsp;<b>b.</b> more generally, <highlightword>that which is outside enclosed cities, the open country</highlightword>, <ref ref=\"Job 18:17\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"17\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"17\" onclick=\"bcv(18,18,17)\">Job 18:17</ref> <bdbheb>וְלאֹ</bdbheb> <bdbheb>שֵׁם לוֺ עַלפְּֿנֵיחֿוּץ</bdbheb> (see <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('De')\">De</lookup>), compare <ref ref=\"Prov 24:27\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"27\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"27\" onclick=\"bcv(20,24,27)\">Prov 24:27</ref> in the plural <ref ref=\"Job 5:10\" b=\"18\" cBegin=\"5\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"5\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(18,5,10)\">Job 5:10</ref> <bdbheb>וְשֹׁלֵחַ מַיִם עַל פְנֵי חוּצוֺת</bdbheb>, <ref ref=\"Prov 8:26\" b=\"20\" cBegin=\"8\" vBegin=\"26\" cEnd=\"8\" vEnd=\"26\" onclick=\"bcv(20,8,26)\">Prov 8:26</ref>; <ref ref=\"Ps 144:13\" b=\"19\" cBegin=\"144\" vBegin=\"13\" cEnd=\"144\" vEnd=\"13\" onclick=\"bcv(19,144,13)\">Ps 144:13</ref> (as place where flocks abound). </p></div><hr>", "references": [{"raw": "Isa 15:3", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 15, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "Deut 23:13", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 23, "verse": 13}, {"raw": "Deut 23:14", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 23, "verse": 14}, {"raw": "Judg 19:25", "book": "JDG", "chapter": 19, "verse": 25}, {"raw": "2Sam 13:18", "book": "2SA", "chapter": 13, "verse": 18}, {"raw": "Neh 13:8", "book": "NEH", "chapter": 13, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Judg 12:9", "book": "JDG", "chapter": 12, "verse": 9}, {"raw": "2Kgs 4:3", "book": "2KI", "chapter": 4, "verse": 3}, {"raw": "2Kgs 4:2", "book": "2KI", "chapter": 4, "verse": 2}, {"raw": "Lev 18:9", "book": "LEV", "chapter": 18, "verse": 9}, {"raw": "Ezek 47:2", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 47, "verse": 2}, {"raw": "Exod 12:46", "book": "EXO", "chapter": 12, "verse": 46}, {"raw": "Prov 5:16", "book": "PRO", "chapter": 5, "verse": 16}, {"raw": "Num 35:4", "book": "NUM", "chapter": 35, "verse": 4}, {"raw": "1Kgs 6:6", "book": "1KI", "chapter": 6, "verse": 6}, {"raw": "Isa 33:7", "book": "ISA", "chapter": 33, "verse": 7}, {"raw": "2Chr 24:8", "book": "2CH", "chapter": 24, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Gen 15:5", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 15, "verse": 5}, {"raw": "Gen 19:17", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 19, "verse": 17}, {"raw": "Gen 24:29", "book": "GEN", "chapter": 24, "verse": 29}, {"raw": "Josh 2:19", "book": "JOS", "chapter": 2, "verse": 19}, {"raw": "1Kgs 8:8", "book": "1KI", "chapter": 8, "verse": 8}, {"raw": "Deut 25:5", "book": "DEU", "chapter": 25, "verse": 5}, {"raw": "Ezek 41:9", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 41, "verse": 9}, {"raw": "Ezek 34:21", "book": "EZK", "chapter": 34, "verse": 21}, {"raw": "Gen 9:22", "book": "GEN", "c